From: Krishna Gudipati <kgudipat@brocade.com>

Resending the patch 1/33 by splitting it into two patches 1a and 1b,
as its not showing up in the linux-scsi mailing list, due to its size.

Change details:
	- This patch is part of the BFA cleanup.
	- Removed the include subdir under BFA and flattened the hierarchy.
	- The .h files under include will be handled as below:
	  Files under:
		- DEFS  - Cleaned up files bfa_defs.h, bfa_defs_svc.h & bfa_defs_fcs.h
				  will be merged to top-level BFA dir.
		- FCB   - FCS call back header files will be removed.
		- FCS   - Files are merged to bfa_fcs.h and this will be merged to top-level.
		- Others:
				- Files bfa.h, bfa_fcpim.h, bfa_svc.h are moved to top-level.
				- bfa timer structure's are merged to bfa_ioc.h and moved to top-level.
				- bfa_fcptm.h is no longer used.

Signed-off-by: Krishna Gudipati <kgudipat@brocade.com>
